    "text": "VERDICT: NOT SUPPORTED. Time in market 69.3%. (a) Mean top-layer forget-gate correlates r=-0.17 with Close/SMA200-1 and r=-0.03 with the 20-day SMA_200 slope (pooled Pearson); median per-fold |r| of cell-state PC1 = 0.69 / 0.54 (placebo 50-day trend: 0.57; a 200-day-specific memory should beat the placebo) -> not met (needs pooled |r|>=0.3 and PC1 |r|>=0.5). (b) in 5 scored OOS crash window(s) the strategy had a shallower MDD than an exposure-matched constant-weight Buy & Hold in 3; mean return -15.38% vs Buy & Hold -34.74%; flat 68.43% of crash days vs 30.71% overall (needs >=10 pp more flat in crashes) -> not met. (c) Removing the 200-day features at test time changes directional accuracy by up to 0.02 pp and MDD by up to 1.81 pp (baseline DA 51.94%, MDD -41.02%) -> not met (needs DA drop >=1 pp or MDD worsening >=2 pp). SKILL CHECK: corr(predicted, actual next-day return) = -0.012; up-day base rate 52.9% (directional accuracy 51.94% is only meaningful relative to it); average daily return when long 10.6 bps vs flat 10.9 bps. TIMING CHECK: strategy Sharpe 0.83 / MDD -41.02% vs a constant 69% Buy & Hold Sharpe 0.96 / MDD -32.37% - lower drawdown than full Buy & Hold is only evidence of skill if it beats this. CAVEATS: the initial training window runs to 2010-10-05 and contains the whole 2008 crash, so no 2008 claim is out-of-sample; the LSTM has 54,081 parameters vs 13,569 for a same-size Simple RNN (capacity confound); trade thresholds are tuned on validation data that also drives early stopping (mild optimism); gate/cell-state correlations between smooth trending series can be spurious and units are not comparable across retrained folds. Heuristic thresholds; 0/3 criteria met."
